        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false">
                <Vermiculite code="1">
                    <English>Unknown</English>
                    <French>Inconnu</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>During the inspection we notice that the seals of the doors were not working properly and therefore a lot of air penetrates into the house. We also notice some leaks through the windows mostly the wood ones. Other than the windows and doors we notice air leakage from the wood box located in the laundry room.



After the infiltration test we proceed to a depressurisation test to verify the capaciy of the ventilation equipment present in the house to create a combustion gases back draft. This situation can be fatal. The result was -7.6 Pa which is over the limit based at -5 Pa. The installation of a Carbon Monoxyde detector is highly recommended  to keep the house safe.</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>During the inspection the owner mention the idea of insulating the garage. This might be  a good occasion to increase the insulation of the adjacent wall.</mainWalls>
                <ceilings>Unfortunately it was impossible to verify the attic insulation because the section was not accessible. According to the age of the house and the heel height we astimate the insulation to be R-40. We recommend to upgrade the roof insulation to the actual standard R-60 or even R-70.</ceilings>
                <ceilingsCathedral />
                <windows>Must of the windows on the main floor are wood units. We recommend the replacement by Energy Star certified windows  for ZONE 3. For more advices for the selection of new windows we recommend to consult a window specialist to find the best product for northern climate.</windows>
                <doors>The weather strippings are not working properly. We recommend the replacement of it, or the replacement of the door. Replacing the door can contribute to keep the house warmer.</doors>
                <Renewables>During the evaluation the owner mention also the idea of installing a solar panel ssystem. The addition of renewable energy will constribute to reduce your energy consumption.</Renewables>
                <AdditionalComments>On the second floor there is a fireplace. This type of heating is not sealed and during the infiltration test we observed a lot of air entering inside the house by the chimney. We the presence of such type of eqquipment you can expect a lot of air draft coming from it specially on cold days. The replacement of the closing of this type of heating is a personal choice from the owner. 

Also the prensece of a fireplace can contribute to the feeling of cold in the house. Not only the air can come through the opening but in the same he's a heat loss spot in the house.</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
        </Options>
